We can use the fact that $|z| = 1$ to write $z = e^{i\theta}$ for some $\theta \in \mathbb{R}$ that is not an integer multiple of $2\pi.$  Then
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{1 - z}
&= \frac{1}{1 - e^{i\theta}} \\
&= \frac{1 - e^{-i\theta}}{(1 - e^{i\theta})(1 - e^{-i\theta})} \\
&= \frac{1 - e^{-i\theta}}{1 - e^{i\theta} - e^{-i\theta} + 1} \\
&= \frac{1 - e^{-i\theta}}{2 - (e^{i\theta} + e^{-i\theta})} \\
&= \frac{1 - e^{-i\theta}}{2 - 2\cos\theta} \\
&= \frac{1 - e^{-i\theta}}{2(1 - \cos\theta)}
\end{align*}
Now, let's consider the real part of this expression.  We have
\begin{align*}
\operatorname{Re}\left(\frac{1}{1 - z}\right)
&= \operatorname{Re}\left(\frac{1 - e^{-i\theta}}{2(1 - \cos\theta)}\right) \\
&= \frac{1}{2(1 - \cos\theta)}\operatorname{Re}(1 - e^{-i\theta}) \\
&= \frac{1}{2(1 - \cos\theta)}\left(1 - \cos(-\theta)\right) \\
&= \frac{1}{2(1 - \cos\theta)}(1 - \cos\theta) \\
&= \frac{1}{2}.
\end{align*}
So, the real part of $\frac{1}{1 - z}$ is $\frac{1}{2}.$</think> <answer> $\frac{1}{2}\text{.}$</answer>

Done with factoring....* scratch paper* Okay, scrap that.  Remember that $|a + bi| = \sqrt{a^{2} + b^{2}}.$</think> <answer>So $|z|^{2} = z\overline{z} = 1,$ which implies $\overline{z} = \frac{1}{z}.$ Now $\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{1 - z} &= \frac{1}{1 - z} \cdot \frac{1 - \overline{z}}{1 - \overline{z}} = \frac{1 - \overline{z}}{1 - z - \overline{z} + z\overline{z}} \\ &= \frac{1 - \overline{z}}{1 - z - \overline{z} + 1} = \frac{1 - \overline{z}}{2 - z - \overline{z}} = \frac{\frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{2}\overline{z}}{1 - \frac{1}{2}z - \frac{1}{2}\overline{z}} \\ &= \frac{\frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{2}\overline{z}}{1 - \frac{1}{2}(z + \overline{z})} = \frac{\frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{2}\overline{z}}{1 - \text{Re}(z)}
\end{align*}$  We know that $z + \overline{z} = 2\text{Re}(z),$ $\text{Re}(z)$ is real, and $|z + \overline{z}| = |\overline{z} + z| = |z + z| = |2z| = 2|z| = 2,$ which implies $|\text{Re}(z)| \leq 1.$  Thus, $\text{Re}(z) \leq 1.$  So $$\text{Real Part} = \boxed{\frac{1}{2} - \frac{1}{2}\overline{z}}.$$</answer>

